  57:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  58:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) The specific SAI interrupts (FIFO request and Overrun underrun interrupt)
  59:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****         will be managed using the macros __HAL_SAI_ENABLE_IT() and __HAL_SAI_DISABLE_IT()
  60:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****         inside the transmit and receive process.
  61:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  62:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****    (@) Make sure that either:
  63:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****        (+@) I2S PLL is configured or
  64:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****        (+@) SAI PLL is configured or
  65:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****        (+@) External clock source is configured after setting correctly
  66:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****             the define constant EXTERNAL_CLOCK_VALUE in the stm32f7xx_hal_conf.h file.
  67:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  68:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) In master Tx mode: enabling the audio block immediately generates the bit clock
  69:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****         for the external slaves even if there is no data in the FIFO, However FS signal
  70:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****         generation is conditioned by the presence of data in the FIFO.
  71:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  72:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  73:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) In master Rx mode: enabling the audio block immediately generates the bit clock
  74:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****         and FS signal for the external slaves.
  75:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  76:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  77:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) It is mandatory to respect the following conditions in order to avoid bad SAI behavior:
  78:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) First bit Offset <= (SLOT size - Data size)
  79:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) Data size <= SLOT size
  80:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) Number of SLOT x SLOT size = Frame length
  81:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) The number of slots should be even when SAI_FS_CHANNEL_IDENTIFICATION is selected.
  82:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  83:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  84:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Three operation modes are available within this driver :
