ARM GAS  /tmp/cc7jkpta.s 			page 4


 146:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 147:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     The compilation define USE_HAL_SAI_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 148:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 149:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Use functions HAL_SAI_RegisterCallback() to register a user callback.
 150:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 151:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 152:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Function HAL_SAI_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 153:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback     : SAI receive complete.
 154:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) RxHalfCpltCallback : SAI receive half complete.
 155:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback     : SAI transmit complete.
 156:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) TxHalfCpltCallback : SAI transmit half complete.
 157:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback      : SAI error.
 158:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SAI MspInit.
 159:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SAI MspDeInit.
 160:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 161:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the callback ID
 162:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     and a pointer to the user callback function.
 163:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 164:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 165:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Use function HAL_SAI_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 166:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     weak function.
 167:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     HAL_SAI_UnRegisterCallback() takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 168:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     and the callback ID.
 169:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 170:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 171:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback     : SAI receive complete.
 172:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) RxHalfCpltCallback : SAI receive half complete.
 173:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback     : SAI transmit complete.
 174:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) TxHalfCpltCallback : SAI transmit half complete.
 175:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback      : SAI error.
 176:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SAI MspInit.
 177:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SAI MspDeInit.
 178:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 179:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 180:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     By default, after the HAL_SAI_Init and if the state is HAL_SAI_STATE_RESET
 181:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     all callbacks are reset to the corresponding legacy weak functions:
 182:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     examples HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback(), HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback().
 183:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit callbacks that are respectively
 184:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     reset to the legacy weak functions in the HAL_SAI_Init
 185:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     and HAL_SAI_DeInit only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 186:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_SAI_Init and HAL_SAI_DeInit
 187:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand).
 188:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 189:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 190:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in READY state only.
 191:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Exception done for MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks that can be registered/unregistered
 192:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     in READY or RESET state, thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used
 193:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     during the Init/DeInit.
 194:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 195:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     using HAL_SAI_RegisterCallback before calling HAL_SAI_DeInit
 196:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     or HAL_SAI_Init function.
 197:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 198:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 199:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     When the compilation define USE_HAL_SAI_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 200:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     not defined, the callback registering feature is not available
 201:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c ****     and weak callbacks are used.
 202:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
